1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,660
My Lord Count Zebron, Countess Raffia, and Count Olga, my gratitude to all of you for allowing me to intrude on your time.

2
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,740
Our condolences to you for your loss, Count Troyard.

3
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:16,300
Most regrettable and quite tragic.

4
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:17,220
Yes.

5
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:23,820
I was very greatly indebted to your late father, the Count. Any assistance in my power to render is yours.

6
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:30,540
Thank you, that is most kind. And with that being said, now is not the time to wallow in sentiment.

7
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:32,320
Most commendable of you.

8
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:38,660
This is the time when all the Orbital Knights should come together and continue with our invasion of the Earth.

9
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:42,600
For Count Sosbohm, that is the finest way we can commemorate him.

10
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:47,900
Right. Everyone among us should sail forward all in pursuit of our goal.

11
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:49,000
I see now.

12
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:53,280
Really? And you intend your hand to be on the helm?

13
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:56,440
If I may be so bold.

14
00:00:57,080 --> 00:01:01,920
Hmm. By the by, I understand you will be dueling Count Morissian.

15
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:06,300
I find it unsettling to be fighting at a time we should unite.

16
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:09,240
Don't you agree, my Lord Count Troyard?

17
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:18,060
It seems that no Terran, no lowly Terran, could ever stand against the mighty verse.

18
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:23,440
Such an assumption creates an opening, which then becomes a tear, and soon after that, a huge hole.

19
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:25,720
And then it disintegrates.

20
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:29,020
This is the state of the Orbital Knights.

21
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:32,740
Now you have gone too far, Count Troyard.

22
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:36,780
As you know, I do not have the advantage of being verse-born.

23
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:40,520
However, as an outsider, I do have a clear perspective.

24
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:47,540
Now this upcoming duel is the result of hubris in a night, and I think it is my duty to point out his mistake.

25
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:51,660
Yes, I see. You do have a point.

26
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:52,640
But Count Olga!

27
00:01:53,400 --> 00:02:00,060
Loath as I am to admit this, it is truth nonetheless. Some portion of it at least.

28
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:04,840
I must trust in your discretion, Count Troyard.

29
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:09,440
Your attack was magnificent against their trident base.

30
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:16,200
Count Zebran, Countess Rathia, you have done me great honor.

31
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:19,320
In hearing me out, I am in your debt.

32
00:02:30,060 --> 00:03:00,040
I am in your debt.

33
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:30,040
I am in your debt.

34
00:03:30,060 --> 00:04:00,040
I am in your debt.

35
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:03,220
Captain, all cruise missiles appear to have been intercepted.

36
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:05,920
Looks like a saturation attack isn't going to work.

37
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:10,340
Data says a cataphrac is scorching Solas, and the pilot is Count Selnakis.

38
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:16,360
Its beam weapon is effective as far as a satellite belt, meaning air support is too vulnerable to be helpful.

39
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:19,020
It is quite the monster.

40
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:22,080
Message from assault team.

41
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:23,820
They're about to make landfall.

42
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:25,540
Launch more cruise missiles.

43
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,180
Let's keep his eyes on us.

44
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:32,620
Looks like up close and personal is how we're going to have to do it.

45
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,040
Let's do this.

46
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:37,440
All right, all pilots up and ready to launch.

47
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:44,600
What's the matter with you?

48
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:58,680
What's the matter with you?

49
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,400
Oh, nothing.

50
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:01,140
Say, Raiye.

51
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:01,980
Yeah?

52
00:05:02,580 --> 00:05:04,900
The other day, there was that manhunt all of a sudden.

53
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:08,540
It was for, um, ma, ma, ma, ma...

54
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:09,420
Count Mazurek.

55
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:10,200
Right.

56
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:12,500
How do you suppose he got away?

57
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:13,860
Don't know.

58
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:16,020
I wonder if Inahu knows anything.

59
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:17,600
Why would he?

60
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:19,220
He interrogated him.

61
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:21,140
Did he say anything to you?

62
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:22,580
Not a word.

63
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:26,920
It's time to launch.

64
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:27,560
Let's go.

65
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:28,320
All right.

66
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:32,220
Inko, I'm sorry.

67
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:41,340
To think such a simple mechanism can show one's bearings.

68
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:44,520
Of course, only on a planet with magnetic poles.

69
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:49,240
Now then, we have Count Troyard and Inaho Kaizuka.

70
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:51,540
Both of them are sons of the Earth.

71
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:53,480
Can either be trusted?

72
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:59,300
It's so simple, one cannot go astray, right?

73
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:02,800
Like many things.

74
00:06:07,660 --> 00:06:11,180
Are you truly going to go out and fight this duel, Slain?

75
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:11,940
Yes.

76
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:15,180
I have been challenged, so I cannot back down.

77
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:18,140
This is my fault, isn't it?

78
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:20,500
Because I allowed Count Morilcion's visit.

79
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:21,600
Not at all.

80
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:23,540
Rather, I have you to thank for it.

81
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:27,460
It is the perfect opportunity to demonstrate my strengths.

82
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:30,240
If I am a victor in this duel,

83
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:33,640
it will be a deterrent to the orbital knights who oppose me.

84
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:36,720
There's nothing to be concerned about.

85
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:43,220
Then your dream might actually become reality someday.

86
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,380
I don't have a dream.

87
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:49,700
A lowly Terran now holds genuine power within verse.

88
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:54,420
I have felt it, ever since the very first time we met,

89
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:57,780
that the two of us were quite similar in some way.

90
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:02,040
Do you intend to hold your grudge against the royal family forever?

91
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:03,480
Yes.

92
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:09,040
How deliciously satisfying to see someone without a drop of Vercyan blood gaining power.

93
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:15,180
And I think that you will never let go either of a Salem.

94
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,800
You truly love her, don't you?

95
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:28,100
Slain, if you were to allow it, I would like to give you my help.

96
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:33,980
Even if I am to be my sister's substitute.

97
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:38,920
All platoons, report.

98
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,800
Belgian platoon, positioned.

99
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,720
Marimano platoon, positioned.

100
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:44,540
Potok platoon, positioned.

101
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:46,520
Wokai platoon, positioned.

102
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,340
Mustang platoon, in position.

103
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:51,220
There's no way around that beam weapon he's got out there.

104
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,400
If he sees you, it'll be goodbye.

105
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:54,900
